CX_DR_TRAP=3: user-mode hardware debug registers under Rosetta 2.

The ninth patch in build.sh's PATCHES list, built into fixes/: FIFA 16's
bottle (AURORA_GAME=fifa16) sets CX_DR_TRAP=3. Applies after the eight
before it (it builds on the CX_DR_TRAP / CX_DR_PERSIST / drcache code in the
rosetta patch). Nothing changes unless a bottle sets CX_DR_TRAP=3; modes 0-2
run the same code as before, so FIFA 17's bottle, on 2, is unaffected.
See README-debug-register-emulation.md for each bug, the tests, and the results.

Rosetta refuses debug registers outright (CW HACK 22131), and stock Wine drops
them without a word: a thread that arms Dr0-3 through SetThreadContext never
sees a breakpoint, and GetThreadContext reads zeros back. Mode 2 (shipped)
covers one pattern only, an execute breakpoint armed by another thread.
Mode 3 emulates the documented x86-64 semantics with page protection:

  execute bp        page loses execute; delivered before the instruction, RF skips it
  write watchpoint  page loses write; the access is stepped over under TF and
                    the #DB is delivered after the instruction
  rw=11 watchpoint  page loses all access. Reads of KUSER_SHARED_DATA are
                    completed inside the fault handler out of a read-only alias
                    of the page, so no protection window ever opens
  Dr6               per event: 0xffff0ff0 | B bits of this hit, BS with a TF step
  Dr7               global-enable bits stripped, as Windows does

and keeps the page games invisible: VirtualQuery reports the page's own
protection, a guest VirtualProtect on a watched page replaces that protection
and is re-stripped underneath, accesses the page itself would deny stay the
guest's access violation, and unix-side reads inside a syscall never raise a
#DB. State lives in a process-wide table (1024 breakpoints, 256 threads, ERR
when full) and is dropped at thread exit so a reused TID inherits nothing.

Files: dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c (the emulation), virtual.c (the
KUSER alias, the query/protect hooks), thread.c (thread-exit cleanup).
Tests: tests/drbp (drrf_test 7/7, drbp_test 7/8; case 3 fails in control too).

